WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.862
Duplicate detection and duplicate resolution are different stages.

00:00:03.862 --> 00:00:07.227
Detection tries to find plausible candidate groups.

00:00:07.227 --> 00:00:09.997
Resolution decides what to do with them.

00:00:09.997 --> 00:00:15.702
That could mean choosing a survivor, merging complementary fields, quarantining the group,

00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:17.867
or sending it for human review.

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:21.562
Separating the stages makes deduplication safer.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:28.087
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:33.482
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.482 --> 00:00:40.672
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.672 --> 00:00:46.187
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:51.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
